[{:seon.task/name "a-model-call-follows-its-config"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-21: \"this was all done before in the configs and the model execution code should follow the configs that are passed.\" Today `seon.config/provider` resolves base URL, key variable and max-tokens through `seon.config/resolve-in` but reads `:seon.config.ai/thinking` and `:seon.config.ai/reasoning-effort` straight from the global config, so a model or a task cannot set them; root builds one provider at start and every call uses it; `seon.model/default-max-tokens` is a second source of max-tokens frozen at namespace load; and `:seon.task/config` admits only `:seon.config.agent/max-turns`. Correct (one resolver, v1's per-model request construction): each model request's settings (model, max-tokens, thinking, reasoning effort) come from `seon.config/resolve` for that request's task and model (task -> model -> provider -> config), `seon.model` builds the request from what it is handed and holds no defaults of its own (`default-max-tokens` deleted), and a task's config may state the `:seon.config.ai/*` keys its model accepts. Minimal code: extend the resolver and the request builder, no second path."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.model-test/a-request-carries-its-tasks-resolved-settings}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-reply-records-its-cached-tokens"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-10-21 on the standing root: attempt `seon.fences/a-refused-spawn-is-recorded#1` took 13 model calls and 4,123,353 tokens (~317k a call), because each turn now resends the conversation under `:seon.config.render/history-budget` 256000. DeepSeek serves a repeated prefix from its context cache at ~2% of the miss price and reports it in the reply's usage (`prompt_cache_hit_tokens`, `prompt_cache_miss_tokens`, api-docs.deepseek.com, context caching), but `seon.model/parse-reply` keeps only prompt and completion tokens, so whether that attempt cost ~$0.01 or ~$0.58 is unknown, and the history budget cannot be set from measurement. Correct: the completion carries the provider's cache-hit and cache-miss prompt tokens when it reports them (absent when not: absent is not 0), the turn records them (`:seon.turn/*`), and the attempt sums them beside its tokens, so `seon.learn`'s rows can show cost per template. Then set the history budget from turns-to-green against cost. Re-read 2026-10-22 (worktree session context-v2): `seon.model/reply-of` already keeps `prompt_cache_hit_tokens` as :cache-hit-tokens and the model call records it as `:seon.fx/cache-hit-tokens`, but it drops `prompt_cache_miss_tokens` and the OpenAI-compatible `prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens`, and the turn records neither (`seon.turn/act!`). Correct: the completion carries :cache-hit-tokens (either field) and :cache-miss-tokens when reported; the turn records `:seon.turn/cache-hit-tokens` and `:seon.turn/cache-miss-tokens` beside `:seon.turn/tokens`, absent when not reported; the attempt's cache share is derived from its turns (R4: grades and rows are derived, never stored)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.model-test/a-reply-reports-its-cache-hit-and-miss-tokens
                      seon.model-test/a-turn-records-what-the-provider-reported}}
 {:seon.task/name "budgets-are-data-and-spend-is-measured"
  :seon.task/plan "Audit FENCES #23-25, #27, #30-31, re-read at 26363fe. Unknown spend is written as 0, so the record says an attempt cost nothing when nobody measured it: `seon.reconcile/judge-tx` (an attempt whose agent wrote no end: died, killed, or never reached `seon.turn/end!`) records outcome :error with :turns, :model-calls and :tokens 0 through `seon.task/end-members`; `seon.model/parse-reply` reads a reply with no usage as 0 prompt and 0 completion tokens; `seon.fx/settle` charges a call that states no cost 1 against the task's spend. Correct: an attempt with no end is outcome :no-end (added to `:seon.attempt/outcome`'s enum in resources/seon/schemas/seon.facts.edn) with its turns, model-calls and tokens absent (`:seon.turn/end` and `seon.task/end-members` take them as optional; `seon.task/end-members` writes only what it was given); a completion without usage has no :prompt-tokens or :completion-tokens (`:seon.model/completion` makes both optional; `seon.fx/model`'s :cost and the turn's `:seon.turn/tokens` are then absent, not 0, and every reader of them, seon.turn's token sum and `seon.fx/settle`, handles the absent count as unknown, not as 0: settle charges nothing it did not measure and the bucket keeps the estimate it reserved). An estimate, where one is shown, is marked :estimated. PREMISES CHANGED since the audit: (1) the dials are no longer code literals; 990cf51 moved them to config keys, but `seon.reconcile/default-max-turns`, `default-max-running`, `default-max-merging`, `merge-dials` and `default-budget` read them once at load and chain task -> default by hand, a second resolver beside `seon.config/resolve-in` that skips the model and provider: census #5, its own task (not this one); (2) the token budget (an attempt's budget in tokens, :cap naming what was spent against what was allowed) is a design question for the owner, since `seon.fx/admit` already refuses a request whose :budget-key spent its :budget (:seon.fx/budget-spent) and nothing sets :budget on a model call: left out of this task until ruled. Estimate: no new work; fewer facts written. Done (session fences-spend, 2026-10-22, moved here from the fences file; its need on the merge-train task dropped, that task landed): `seon.reconcile/judge-tx` also copied :model-calls from :turns; it now takes turns, model-calls and tokens only from the end the agent wrote (`seon.reconcile/pull-end` reads no model-calls, so they stay absent until an end records them) and an attempt with no end is `:no-end`; `seon.task/end-members` writes only the counts it was given; `seon.model/parse-reply` leaves out a count the provider did not send, and the stand-in's counts (`seon.print.select/estimate`) are marked `:estimated`; `seon.fx/model` states `:cost` only when both counts are known and `seon.fx/settle` charges nothing unmeasured (the bucket keeps its reservation); `seon.turn`'s act! sums a turn's tokens only when known (one unknown turn makes the attempt's total unknown). Left for root: `seon.e2e`'s summaries still read an absent count as 0 (`(:seon.attempt/model-calls % 0)`)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.reconcile-test/an-attempt-with-no-end-records-no-fake-spend
                      seon.model-test/a-reply-without-usage-records-no-tokens}}]
